===Etymology===
{{etyl|la|en}} {{term/t|la|Cerēs}}, goddess of the bounty, akin to {{term/t|la|crēare||to create}}, {{term/t|la|crēscere||to grow}}, from {{etyl|ine-pro|en}} {{term/t|ine-pro|*ḱer-||to grow}}. More at [[create]].

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈsɪəriːz/|lang=en}}

===Proper noun===
{{en-proper noun}}

# {{context|Roman god|lang=en}} The Roman [[goddess]] of [[agriculture]]; equivalent to the [[Greek]] goddess [[Demeter]].
# {{context|astronomy|lang=en}} A celestial body [[orbit]]ing between [[Mars]] and [[Jupiter]], the largest [[asteroid]] and innermost [[dwarf planet]]; officially called {{term|1 Ceres|1 '''Ceres'''}}.

